  "title": "Adjective endings",
  "description": "How dobry (good) changes with gender, number and case.",
  "sections": [
    {
      "text": "Adjectives agree with their noun in gender, number and case. After k, g and soft consonants, -y becomes -i: polski, drogi, tani.",
      "table": {
        "columns": ["Case", "Masculine", "Feminine", "Neuter", "Plural (men)", "Plural (others)"],
        "rows": [
          ["Nominative", "dobry", "dobra", "dobre", "dobrzy", "dobre"],
          ["Genitive", "dobrego", "dobrej", "dobrego", "dobrych", "dobrych"],
          ["Dative", "dobremu", "dobrej", "dobremu", "dobrym", "dobrym"],
          [
            "Accusative",
            "dobry (thing), dobrego (person, animal)",
            "dobrą",
            "dobre",
            "dobrych",
            "dobre"
          ],
          ["Instrumental", "dobrym", "dobrą", "dobrym", "dobrymi", "dobrymi"],
          ["Locative", "dobrym", "dobrej", "dobrym", "dobrych", "dobrych"]
        ]
      },
      "examples": [
        {
          "text": "To dobra książka.",
          "translation": "It is a good book."
        },
        {
          "text": "Mam dobrego przyjaciela.",
          "translation": "I have a good friend."
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
